WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.534 --> 00:00:06.039
"Is Ozempic (Semaglutide) Safe?"

00:00:07.441 --> 00:00:08.976
GLP-1 weight-loss drugs.

00:00:08.976 --> 00:00:11.678
How safe are they?

00:00:11.678 --> 00:00:13.947
Regulatory authorities
have expressed concerns

00:00:13.947 --> 00:00:17.417
about the potential risk
of acute pancreatitis,

00:00:17.417 --> 00:00:20.087
thyroid cancer,
and kidney failure,

00:00:20.087 --> 00:00:21.655
warnings that are
appropriately conveyed

00:00:21.655 --> 00:00:25.025
in every box of drugs
handed to a patient.

00:00:25.025 --> 00:00:27.427
Here’s the actual package insert
for high-dose Ozempic,

00:00:27.427 --> 00:00:29.696
sold for weight loss as Wegovy.

00:00:29.696 --> 00:00:33.400
Warnings and precautions
include thyroid tumors,

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:34.968
acute inflammation
of the pancreas,

00:00:34.968 --> 00:00:36.169
acute gallbladder disease,

00:00:36.169 --> 00:00:37.905
heightened risk
of low blood sugars

00:00:37.905 --> 00:00:39.940
if you’re on blood
sugar-lowering medications,

00:00:39.940 --> 00:00:42.376
acute kidney injury,
allergic reactions,

00:00:42.376 --> 00:00:45.078
worsening eye disease
for those with type 2 diabetes,

00:00:45.078 --> 00:00:47.247
an increase in heart rate
that should be monitored,

00:00:47.247 --> 00:00:49.917
and suicidal thoughts
and behaviors.

00:00:49.917 --> 00:00:50.851
And the package insert

00:00:50.851 --> 00:00:52.986
for the other major
GLP-1 weight loss drug,

00:00:52.986 --> 00:00:54.988
tirzepatide, sold as Zepbound,

00:00:54.988 --> 00:00:57.791
reads almost word for word
the same.

00:00:57.791 --> 00:01:02.029
Let’s start with the good news,
suicide.

00:01:02.029 --> 00:01:05.632
The possibility of an adverse
psychiatric event on GLP-1 drugs

00:01:05.632 --> 00:01:07.434
is biologically plausible

00:01:07.434 --> 00:01:10.070
because GLP-1 receptors
are widely expressed

00:01:10.070 --> 00:01:12.739
in the central nervous system,
including our brain.

00:01:12.739 --> 00:01:15.609
So, what does the science show?

00:01:15.609 --> 00:01:18.111
This meta-analysis
of randomized controlled trials

00:01:18.111 --> 00:01:20.180
did not highlight
any detrimental effect

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:23.483
on these drugs on mental health,
including suicide.

00:01:23.483 --> 00:01:25.752
Now, this meta-analysis
only covered studies

00:01:25.752 --> 00:01:28.922
up through the end of 2023
and only clinical trials,

00:01:28.922 --> 00:01:30.691
and those with mental illnesses

00:01:30.691 --> 00:01:33.260
are usually excluded
from such studies.

00:01:33.260 --> 00:01:34.661
But there have been
newer studies done

00:01:34.661 --> 00:01:36.363
with subjects
out in the real world,

00:01:36.363 --> 00:01:39.066
and again,
no clear increased risk.

00:01:39.066 --> 00:01:40.600
And this study,
on the association

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:42.269
of the Ozempic drug semaglutide

00:01:42.269 --> 00:01:45.339
with risk of suicidal ideation
in another cohort

00:01:45.339 --> 00:01:46.740
found that the drug
was associated

00:01:46.740 --> 00:01:48.108
with a lower risk

00:01:48.108 --> 00:01:50.610
for incident and recurrent
suicidal ideation,

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:52.412
apparently cutting
suicidal thoughts

00:01:52.412 --> 00:01:54.181
by more than half,
compared to those

00:01:54.181 --> 00:01:57.117
on the older, less effective
weight-loss drugs.

00:01:57.117 --> 00:01:59.052
After all,
a weight-reducing treatment

00:01:59.052 --> 00:02:00.721
that limits
the burden of obesity

00:02:00.721 --> 00:02:02.656
could improve mood.

00:02:02.656 --> 00:02:06.693
I told you suicide
was the good news!

00:02:06.693 --> 00:02:09.730
Now, on to cancer.

00:02:09.730 --> 00:02:13.166
Both Wegovy, high-dose Ozempic,
and Zepbound (tirzepatide),

00:02:13.166 --> 00:02:15.469
carry so-called
black box warnings

00:02:15.469 --> 00:02:17.537
for thyroid cancer risk.

00:02:17.537 --> 00:02:18.505
Black box warnings

00:02:18.505 --> 00:02:20.273
are the U.S. Food
and Drug Administration’s

00:02:20.273 --> 00:02:21.508
strictest caution

00:02:21.508 --> 00:02:24.211
about potentially
life-threatening hazards.

00:02:24.211 --> 00:02:26.646
In rodents, these drugs
cause dose-dependent

00:02:26.646 --> 00:02:28.815
and duration-dependent
thyroid tumors

00:02:28.815 --> 00:02:30.917
at clinically relevant
exposures,

00:02:30.917 --> 00:02:33.286
meaning the kind of doses
prescribed to humans.

00:02:33.286 --> 00:02:35.722
Now, we don’t know yet
whether these drugs cause

00:02:35.722 --> 00:02:39.026
a thyroid cancer called
medullary thyroid carcinoma,

00:02:39.026 --> 00:02:42.329
which is a cancer of
the thyroid C cells in humans.

00:02:42.329 --> 00:02:43.196
To be on the safe side,

00:02:43.196 --> 00:02:44.865
the drugs shouldn’t
be prescribed

00:02:44.865 --> 00:02:46.066
for high-risk individuals,

00:02:46.066 --> 00:02:48.235
like those with a personal
or family history

00:02:48.235 --> 00:02:49.903
of thyroid cancer,

00:02:49.903 --> 00:02:52.339
but it’s not like the rats
had thyroid cancer

00:02:52.339 --> 00:02:54.041
running in their families.

00:02:54.041 --> 00:02:55.942
Doctors should counsel
their patients

00:02:55.942 --> 00:02:58.879
to remain alert
for symptoms of thyroid tumors,

00:02:58.879 --> 00:03:00.614
like a lump
or swelling in the neck,

00:03:00.614 --> 00:03:02.616
trouble swallowing,
shortness of breath,

00:03:02.616 --> 00:03:05.018
or persistent hoarseness.

00:03:05.018 --> 00:03:08.055
I’d be curious in the comments
to see if any viewers

00:03:08.055 --> 00:03:09.356
who’ve been prescribed
these drugs

00:03:09.356 --> 00:03:13.460
were told any of this
by their prescribing physicians.

00:03:13.460 --> 00:03:15.195
Can’t we just ultrasound
people’s necks

00:03:15.195 --> 00:03:18.098
to see if they develop
thyroid tumors on these drugs?

00:03:18.098 --> 00:03:20.133
That’s considered to be
of uncertain value,

00:03:20.133 --> 00:03:23.003
since no such studies
have been done.

00:03:23.003 --> 00:03:25.105
Now, there have been
studies done

00:03:25.105 --> 00:03:26.840
on GLP-1 drugs, like Ozempic,

00:03:26.840 --> 00:03:29.109
and the risk of thyroid cancer
in people.

00:03:29.109 --> 00:03:32.379
This was the first major one
raising concern,

00:03:32.379 --> 00:03:34.681
published in 2023.

00:03:34.681 --> 00:03:37.784
Researchers found increased risk
of all thyroid cancers

00:03:37.784 --> 00:03:40.020
and specifically,
medullary thyroid cancer

00:03:40.020 --> 00:03:41.755
in people using these drugs,

00:03:41.755 --> 00:03:44.424
particularly after taking them
for a few years.

00:03:44.424 --> 00:03:47.260
A commentary
citing the study asked,

00:03:47.260 --> 00:03:49.629
"Is it the time
to be concerned?"

00:03:49.629 --> 00:03:51.832
Maybe that one study
was just a fluke?

00:03:51.832 --> 00:03:54.334
No, after putting together
all the best studies,

00:03:54.334 --> 00:03:56.269
a systematic review
and meta-analysis

00:03:56.269 --> 00:03:58.572
of randomized controlled trials
found, again,

00:03:58.572 --> 00:04:00.707
a significant increase
in the risk

00:04:00.707 --> 00:04:05.045
of overall thyroid cancer,
about 52 percent greater odds.

00:04:05.045 --> 00:04:08.215
That sounds bad,
until you realize

00:04:08.215 --> 00:04:11.284
just how rare
the cancer is overall.

00:04:11.284 --> 00:04:14.221
The incidence of thyroid cancer
in this kind of population

00:04:14.221 --> 00:04:18.925
is 0.285 cases
per 1,000 patient years.

00:04:18.925 --> 00:04:21.261
This means that
over a span of 10 years,

00:04:21.261 --> 00:04:23.930
we’d only expect
about three people out of 1,000

00:04:23.930 --> 00:04:25.265
to get that cancer.

00:04:25.265 --> 00:04:28.401
So, even if you bump up
that risk by 50 percent,

00:04:28.401 --> 00:04:31.371
you’re still only talking
about four in 1,000

00:04:31.371 --> 00:04:34.040
getting it over a decade,
compared to three in 1,000

00:04:34.040 --> 00:04:36.176
if you hadn’t started
taking the drugs.

00:04:36.176 --> 00:04:40.547
That translates to a five-year
"number needed to harm"

00:04:40.547 --> 00:04:42.682
of 1,349.

00:04:42.682 --> 00:04:45.919
That means that even if this
were truly cause-and-effect,

00:04:45.919 --> 00:04:49.956
it would take treating
1,349 people for five years

00:04:49.956 --> 00:04:53.226
to cause a single additional
case of thyroid cancer.

00:04:54.628 --> 00:04:57.964
And even if you’re
the unlucky soul who gets it,

00:04:57.964 --> 00:05:00.433
it’s pretty mild, as cancers go.

00:05:00.433 --> 00:05:02.135
The five-year
relative survival rate,

00:05:02.135 --> 00:05:04.404
meaning the likelihood
you’ll still be alive

00:05:04.404 --> 00:05:06.239
five years after diagnosis

00:05:06.239 --> 00:05:07.774
compared to people
without the cancer

00:05:07.774 --> 00:05:10.710
is 98.4 percent.

00:05:10.710 --> 00:05:13.713
Okay, but what about the risk
of pancreatic cancer

00:05:13.713 --> 00:05:14.981
with the use of these drugs?

00:05:14.981 --> 00:05:17.017
That has a relative
five-year survival rate

00:05:17.017 --> 00:05:20.120
of only 12.8 percent.

00:05:20.120 --> 00:05:22.923
You can see the difference
between the incidence rates

00:05:22.923 --> 00:05:24.424
and the death rates.

00:05:24.424 --> 00:05:25.759
For thyroid cancer,

00:05:25.759 --> 00:05:27.594
a bunch of people are
diagnosed with it,

00:05:27.594 --> 00:05:29.663
but very few die from it,

00:05:29.663 --> 00:05:31.064
whereas for pancreatic cancer,

00:05:31.064 --> 00:05:33.667
almost everyone who gets it
dies from it.

00:05:33.667 --> 00:05:36.303
So, do these drugs cause
pancreatic cancer?

00:05:36.303 --> 00:05:40.340
That’s exactly the question
I’ll address next.

